      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The tension between avoiding over-censorship of political discourse and preventing actual harm remains unresolved with no consensus on a \"best\" approach. However, recent trends suggest a shift toward more aggressive, AI-assisted moderation to proactively filter hate speech while maintaining manual appeals processes for edge cases. Sticking to a purely hands-off approach often exposes platforms to significant legal risks and public trust issues as hate speech scales online, making a balanced, risk-mitigated strategy more sustainable for a new entry into the market.",
